WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.836
Your best marketing audience is people who already bought from you.

00:00:04.836 --> 00:00:09.356
This video shows how the Marketing module groups your customers into segments by

00:00:09.356 --> 00:00:13.613
what they bought, and sends email campaigns to a segment, only to customers

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:15.400
who agreed to hear from you.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.948
Your orders already say who your customers are:

00:00:22.948 --> 00:00:27.009
who bought last week, who has not bought for months, who buys again

00:00:27.009 --> 00:00:29.290
and again, and who spends the most.

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:32.957
Each of them deserves a different message:

00:00:32.957 --> 00:00:36.846
a thank you to a new customer, an offer to a lapsed buyer,

00:00:36.846 --> 00:00:39.520
an early look for your best customers.

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:44.295
But only customers who agreed to hear from you should get it, and

00:00:44.295 --> 00:00:47.470
each email must let them unsubscribe in one click.

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:53.595
The Marketing module reads your paid orders, groups customers into segments, and sends

00:00:53.595 --> 00:00:56.400
campaigns to them, respecting that choice.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:04.789
A segment is a group of customers that meet rules about their orders,

00:01:04.789 --> 00:01:08.140
such as customers who have not ordered in ninety days.

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:13.252
A campaign is an email that you write for a segment, and send

00:01:13.252 --> 00:01:14.750
now or at a time.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:19.782
A campaign only goes to customers who ticked Send me news and offers,

00:01:19.782 --> 00:01:22.522
or whom you marked as accepting marketing.

00:01:22.522 --> 00:01:25.320
Emails about their orders are not affected.

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:29.133
Every email carries a link to unsubscribe.

00:01:29.133 --> 00:01:33.920
Once a customer confirms, no campaign or review request reaches them.

00:01:38.108 --> 00:01:40.151
Open Commerce, Segments.

00:01:40.151 --> 00:01:44.852
Each segment shows its rules, and how many customers meet them.

00:01:44.852 --> 00:01:46.488
Click Add segment.

00:01:46.966 --> 00:01:52.316
Give it a Name, such as Repeat buyers, and a Description that only your staff see.

00:01:53.069 --> 00:01:56.268
Fill in the rules the customers have to meet.

00:01:56.268 --> 00:02:00.973
Every rule you fill in has to hold, and a rule left blank is ignored.

00:02:00.973 --> 00:02:04.109
Haven't ordered in days finds lapsed buyers.

00:02:04.109 --> 00:02:07.183
Ordered in the last days finds recent ones.

00:02:07.183 --> 00:02:10.759
First ordered in the last days finds new customers.

00:02:11.283 --> 00:02:14.829
At least and At most orders find repeat buyers.

00:02:14.829 --> 00:02:19.646
Spent at least and Spent at most find your best customers, in your

00:02:19.646 --> 00:02:22.122
store's currency, less refunds.

00:02:22.122 --> 00:02:25.133
Country is where their last order went.

00:02:25.607 --> 00:02:26.627
Click Save.

00:02:26.627 --> 00:02:30.767
The segment shows how many customers are in it, and how many of

00:02:30.767 --> 00:02:34.007
them accept marketing, and so get its campaigns.

00:02:38.307 --> 00:02:40.485
Open Commerce, Campaigns.

00:02:40.485 --> 00:02:43.858
It lists your campaigns with their status:

00:02:43.858 --> 00:02:47.371
Draft, Scheduled, Sending, Sent or Canceled.

00:02:47.371 --> 00:02:49.127
Click Add campaign.

00:02:49.649 --> 00:02:51.085
Name the campaign.

00:02:51.085 --> 00:02:52.879
Only staff see the name.

00:02:52.879 --> 00:02:56.229
Choose its Segment, the customers who will get it.

00:02:56.706 --> 00:02:58.623
Write the Subject and the Email.

00:02:58.623 --> 00:03:01.498
The help under the field lists what you can put in:

00:03:01.498 --> 00:03:05.533
the customer's name, how many orders they placed and what they spent, your

00:03:05.533 --> 00:03:09.366
store's name, and their unsubscribe link, which is added at the end if

00:03:09.366 --> 00:03:10.526
you leave it out.

00:03:11.111 --> 00:03:15.698
To check it, enter your address under Send a test to, and click Send test.

00:03:15.698 --> 00:03:17.532
Nothing goes to customers:

00:03:17.532 --> 00:03:21.603
it is filled in as the segment's first customer would get it, and

00:03:21.603 --> 00:03:22.921
sent only to you.

00:03:23.379 --> 00:03:24.481
Click Send.

00:03:24.481 --> 00:03:29.082
Fill in Send at first to send it later, in your site's time zone.

00:03:29.082 --> 00:03:31.999
Or click Save draft to finish it later.

00:03:33.218 --> 00:03:37.598
A campaign goes out in batches over the next minutes, to the segment's

00:03:37.598 --> 00:03:40.421
customers as they are when each batch goes.

00:03:40.421 --> 00:03:44.224
Its page shows how many it was sent to, how many it skipped,

00:03:44.224 --> 00:03:48.892
because they have no email or do not accept marketing, and how many failed.

00:03:48.892 --> 00:03:50.908
Cancel the campaign stops it.

00:03:55.088 --> 00:03:58.525
Customers choose Send me news and offers in their account.

00:03:58.525 --> 00:04:03.197
You can also tick Accepts marketing on a customer, under Commerce, Customers, for

00:04:03.197 --> 00:04:05.238
someone who agreed on the phone.

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:11.080
The unsubscribe link in each email opens a page that asks the customer to confirm.

00:04:11.557 --> 00:04:16.340
Once they confirm, they no longer accept marketing, and no campaign or review

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:17.896
request goes to them.

00:04:17.896 --> 00:04:21.757
They can tick Send me news and offers again in their account.

00:04:25.985 --> 00:04:27.638
Open Tools, Recipes.

00:04:27.638 --> 00:04:31.007
Three recipes add workflows that email for you.

00:04:31.007 --> 00:04:32.088
Automation:

00:04:32.088 --> 00:04:37.365
thank-you email emails each buyer a short thank you when their order is paid.

00:04:37.822 --> 00:04:38.906
Automation:

00:04:38.906 --> 00:04:44.007
canceled order alert emails the store when an order is canceled, with why.

00:04:44.007 --> 00:04:45.091
Automation:

00:04:45.091 --> 00:04:49.936
low stock alert emails the store when a product runs low or sells out.

00:04:49.936 --> 00:04:51.977
Both are added turned off:

00:04:51.977 --> 00:04:55.292
set the address they go to, then turn them on.

00:04:55.746 --> 00:04:58.504
Click Run beside a recipe, and confirm.

00:04:58.504 --> 00:05:01.447
The recipe adds its workflow to your site.

00:05:01.447 --> 00:05:05.002
Then open Tools, Workflows, and find it in the list.

00:05:05.002 --> 00:05:09.048
Open it there to change what the email says, who it goes to,

00:05:09.048 --> 00:05:12.236
and when it is sent, and to turn it on or off.

00:05:16.436 --> 00:05:17.957
A win-back campaign:

00:05:17.957 --> 00:05:22.172
a segment of customers who have not ordered in ninety days, and an

00:05:22.172 --> 00:05:23.636
offer to come back.

00:05:24.386 --> 00:05:25.614
A welcome series:

00:05:25.614 --> 00:05:29.621
customers who first ordered in the last thirty days, and a note about

00:05:29.621 --> 00:05:32.186
how to get the most from what they bought.

00:05:32.936 --> 00:05:34.942
A thank-you for loyalty:

00:05:34.942 --> 00:05:41.096
repeat buyers, or customers who spent at least five hundred, invited to an early sale.

00:05:41.846 --> 00:05:43.343
A local promotion:

00:05:43.343 --> 00:05:48.586
customers whose last order went to one country, with an offer for that market.

00:05:50.586 --> 00:05:54.483
With the Marketing module, you write to the customers who bought, about what

00:05:54.483 --> 00:05:56.860
they bought, and only the ones who said yes.

00:05:56.860 --> 00:05:58.096
Thanks for watching.

